  "note": "The optimisation implementation matches production. After the production audit, self-test assertions were corrected to use reference-distance intervals and the campaign runner gained a no-op guard for a completed archive. The post-campaign changes are recorded separately. The final editorial revision adds a dataset-based Frechet coupling illustration and simplifies plot panel labels. Search code and production records are unchanged. Paired-seed bootstrap confidence intervals quantify stochastic-run variability conditional on the fixed instance suite.",
  "driver_diagnostic": "Post-processing of 3,240 existing main-study plans; optimisation and campaign archive unchanged.",
  "publication_metadata": "Two explicitly identified metadata files have local executable paths made repository-relative. Historical distance-reference JSON lines are represented as a JSON object with a launches array. Original source hashes and transformed file hashes are both retained. Scientific records, source digests and launch parameters are unchanged."
